{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>For she covered her face.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): because she covered her face, he took her for a harlot, for such is the way of harlots to cover their faces, so that they may prostitute themselves even with relatives and not be recognized." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash: כי כסתה פניה — she covered her face in her father-in-law's house, meaning that she had never uncovered her face in Judah's house, and therefore Judah did not recognize her. On this the Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: a person should always be modest with his relatives."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:34.876898146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}